Stop only playback children tracked by this reader

Downstream safety fix for lue 0.5.0; not submitted upstream.
The existing helpers already stop their tracked playback children. Global
pkill patterns additionally terminate unrelated same-user ffplay processes
on navigation and shutdown. Remove only those two global kill blocks,
retaining tracked-child cancellation/termination, queue and buffer cleanup.

Original source: https://github.com/paulilaaso/lue/tree/v0.5.0/lue
Canonical HEAD still contains both blocks as of this audit.

--- a/lue/input_handler.py
+++ b/lue/input_handler.py
@@ -239,5 +238,0 @@
-    try:
-        subprocess.run(['pkill', '-f', 'ffplay'], check=False, 
-                     stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
-    except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, FileNotFoundError):
-        pass
--- a/lue/audio.py
+++ b/lue/audio.py
@@ -66,4 +65,0 @@
-    try:
-        pkill_proc = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec('pkill', '-9', '-f', 'ffplay.*buffer_', stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
-        await asyncio.wait_for(pkill_proc.wait(), timeout=0.3)
-    except (FileNotFoundError, asyncio.TimeoutError): pass
